{
  "correction_rules": [
    "Persistent positive bias: model is systematically too high versus realized prices across the whole 30d horizon (often by ~5–10 EUR, occasionally more). Apply a downward level shift to the entire forecast path.",
    "Downtrend underreaction / lag: when history rolls over from highs to a decline, the model path falls too slowly (forecasts stay near prior regime). Increase sensitivity to recent negative momentum (e.g., weight last 5–10 days more) and steepen early-horizon declines.",
    "Insufficient mean reversion after peaks: following elevated history (80s), the model expects stabilization/rebound while outcomes continue reverting lower (into high 60s/low 70s). Add stronger mean-reversion toward a lower short-term equilibrium after a peak regime.",
    "Horizon-shaped error: largest overprediction tends to appear in the 1–15 day window (model keeps prices in mid/high-70s while realized quickly drops to low-70s/high-60s). Use a larger negative correction for short horizons, smaller (but still negative) for later horizons.",
    "False rebound/overshoot late horizon: model often introduces a late-horizon recovery (days ~20–30) that does not materialize (realized stays flat-to-down). Damp late-horizon upward slopes unless confirmed by recent upward momentum."
  ]
}
